{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ConcaveOnSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ConcaveOnSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Function","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.StrictConcaveOn.sum_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.StrictConcaveOn.sum_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ConcaveOnSum.lean#L84-L98","doc":"**One strictly concave summand makes the whole sum strictly concave**, provided the\nothers are concave.\n\nThis is the form the triangulation argument needs: see the module docstring for why\nasking all summands to be strictly concave would be the wrong hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ConvexOn.sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ConvexOn.sum","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ConcaveOnSum.lean#L71-L82","doc":"**A `Finset`-indexed sum of convex functions is convex.** The dual of\n`ConcaveOn.sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ConcaveOn.sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ConcaveOn.sum","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ConcaveOnSum.lean#L56-L69","doc":"**A `Finset`-indexed sum of concave functions is concave.**\n\nStated with the hypothesis as an arrow so that `induction t` needs no manual\ngeneralisation — the family hypothesis mentions `t`, so it has to travel with it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}